 E appearance_gift_owed {'en': "the appearance gift owed — the DEBIT the migrated clause writes on the pilgrim: 'and they shall not appear before Me empty' — at the first seat closing the matzah feast (23:15), at the second closing the firstborn's redemption (34:20): the appearance burnt offering (Mishnah Chagigah 1:2's amounts the data channel), read where it now stands as the son's standing redemption (Bekhorot 51b) and exported to the slave's severance gift (Kiddushin 17a)", 'he': 'וְלֹֽא יֵרָאוּ פָנַי רֵיקָֽם (and they shall not appear before Me empty — Exod 34:20)', 'ledger_op': 'debit', 'ink': "Exod 34:20 ('they shall not appear before Me empty' at Exod 23:15 and 34:20 alone — the clause MOVED between the two seats; 'every firstborn of your sons you shall redeem' — 'tifdeh' three times in the verse), 23:15 (the first seat, after the matzah feast), 34:23 ('three times in the year all your males shall appear' — 23:17's 'to the face' written 'the face of the Lord, the God of Israel' here); Deut 16:16-17 ('they shall not appear before the LORD empty; each according to the gift of his hand' — the third seat with its measure clause); Onkelos Exod 34:18-26 ('none appear EMPTY-HANDED'); Babylonian Talmud Bekhorot 51b:8, 51b:11, Kiddushin 17a:7, 29b:5, Chagigah 6a:14-15", 'corpus': 'exo_34_second_tablets (STEP_Ex_34_20, 34_23); exo_23_justice_calendar (STEP_Ex_23_15, 23_17)', 'exam': 'cold_run_erection.py; cold_run_calendar.py (pilgrimage — appearance_owed, the duty); Mishnah Chagigah 1:1-2, 1:5-6 (the appearing, its two amounts, its window), Bekhorot 8:7 (the five selas)'}
