 E place_chosen_required {'en': "the place chosen required — the STATUS the line place_chosen_declared writes on Israel: 'BUT TO THE PLACE WHICH THE LORD YOUR GOD WILL CHOOSE FROM ALL YOUR TRIBES TO PUT HIS NAME THERE — HIS DWELLING YOU SHALL SEEK, and there you shall come; and you shall bring there your burnt offerings and your sacrifices, your tithes and the heave offering of your hand, your vows and your freewill offerings, and the firstlings of your herd and of your flock' (12:5-6); 'then the place which the LORD your God will choose to make His name dwell there — there you shall bring all that I command you' (12:11); 'in the place which the LORD will choose in one of your tribes' (12:14) — THE PLACE INSTALLED HERE ('will choose' none before the chapter; 'to put His name there' and 'to make His name dwell there' the two forms; His dwelling the Bible's one seat, the Shekhinah supplied by Onkelos; the two seekings — His dwelling sought, 12:5, and the place found, 12:11): THE VALUE FROM THE SHELF — THE NAME PRONOUNCED ONLY THERE (Mishnah Sotah 7:6 — the priestly blessing's Name as written in the Temple, by its substitute in the provinces; Sotah 38a:10 by the verbal analogy 'to put His name there'; 38a:11 R. Yoshiya's TRANSPOSITION of Exodus 20:20 'in every place where I cause My name to be mentioned I will come to you' read 'in every place where I come to you — the Temple — you may mention My name'); 'IN ONE OF YOUR TRIBES' [1] — the ground from one tribe (Benjamin's strip, Zevachim 118b:6-12; 33:12 ahead), the money from all (the Sifrei 62:2-3, 70:4); THE SEVEN OFFERINGS' THREE LISTS (12:6, 12:11 with 'the choice of your vows' — 68:6 Shiloh's and Jerusalem's; 12:17) — the first fruits for the heave offering of the hand (63:9); 'there — thither' two partitions (67:4); THE STATIONS the eras table's own ink — the six rows read by CALL, unmoved; the second tithe at Nob and Gibeon disputed (Zevachim 119a:7-8 — 'three temples'); THE REST AND THE INHERITANCE four ways (119a:9-13, 119b:1-5) — 12:9 the STATE ROW, no write; the answer sheet's order following the chapter's (Rambam's Introduction 15:74-75); 12:10-11 'when He gives you rest … then the place' — THE INSTALL HYPOTHESIS's own ink (the installer boot as the form; a DATA row); David's rest before the seeking of the site (2 Samuel 7:1; Sanhedrin 20b:14)", 'he': 'אֶל הַמָּקוֹם אֲשֶׁר יִבְחַר יְהוָה אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶם מִכָּל שִׁבְטֵיכֶם לָשׂוּם אֶת שְׁמוֹ שָׁם (to the place which the LORD your God will choose from all your tribes to put His name there — Deut 12:5)', 'ledger_op': 'status', 'ink': "Deut 12:5-6, 12:11, 12:14 (the place and the offerings), 12:9-10 (the rest and the inheritance — the state row), 12:18, 12:21, 12:26 (the place's other seats in the chapter); Deut 14:23-25, 16:2-16, 17:8, 26:2 (the formula ahead); Exodus 20:20 (the transposition — ordinances.altar by CALL), 40:17 (erected on the tape — the tabernacle stood); Leviticus 17:8-9 (sanctions.outside by CALL); Numbers 10:33 (beha.march by CALL — the rest of the ark); Onkelos 12:5; Mishnah Zevachim 14:4-8; Mishnah Sotah 7:6; Mishnah Megillah 1:10-11; Mishnah Yoma 1:1; Babylonian Talmud Zevachim 112b-119b, Sotah 37b-38b, Megillah 9b-10a, Sanhedrin 20b, Rosh Hashanah 4a-6b, Pesachim 8b; 2 Samuel 7:1; Joshua 21:42, 23:1; the Sifrei on Deuteronomy 62-70", 'corpus': 'deu_12_place_name (STEP_Dt_12_5, STEP_Dt_12_6, STEP_Dt_12_9 through STEP_Dt_12_11, STEP_Dt_12_14; the claims DV12-01 through DV12-06)', 'exam': "cold_run_place_name.py (F2 the_place_chosen — the_place_which_the_lord_will_choose, the_name_pronounced_only_there, in_one_of_your_tribes, the_seven_offerings, the_stations_six_rows, the_rest_and_the_inheritance, the_three_commandments_of_the_entry, the_second_answer_sheet; F3 the_burnt_offerings_only_there; the exam kind place_name_case; the status written on the tape kind place_chosen_declared at the counter's day)"}
 E burn_remainder {'en': "burn what remains — the leftover leaves the world by fire; a duty on the object's holder", 'he': 'וְהַנֹּתָר מִמֶּנּוּ עַד בֹּקֶר בָּאֵשׁ תִּשְׂרֹפוּ (and that which remains of it until morning you shall burn with fire)', 'ledger_op': 'transfer', 'ink': 'Exod 12:10 (תשרפו machine-verified)', 'corpus': 'exo_12_passover_and_exodus; the positive-after-negative cluster (Pesachim 83b-84a, triage rows)', 'exam': "cases from the backfill's leaven/leftover rows"}
 E counts_omer {'en': "counts the omer — the forty-nine-day count from the sheaf's morrow, each person's own timer, the fiftieth day the festival", 'he': 'וּסְפַרְתֶּם לָכֶם (and you shall count for yourselves); שֶׁבַע שַׁבָּתוֹת תְּמִימֹת (seven whole weeks)', 'ledger_op': 'timer', 'ink': 'Lev 23:15-16 (probe וספרתם fired; חמשים at 23:16)', 'corpus': 'lev_23_spring_festivals (LV23A-10 — reap and count by night, bring by day; count forty-nine, sanctify the fiftieth)', 'exam': "emor exam module calendar_spring_file (Mishnah Menachot 10:5 the new-grain clock keyed to the count's first day)"}
 E dwells_in_booths {'en': 'dwells in booths — the seven-day dwelling obligation on every native, nights as days by the installation analogy', 'he': 'בַּסֻּכֹּת תֵּשְׁבוּ שִׁבְעַת יָמִים (in booths you shall dwell seven days)', 'ledger_op': 'timer', 'ink': 'Lev 23:42 (probe תשבו fired; סכת twice in the verse)', 'corpus': 'lev_23_fall_festivals (LV23B-11 — dwell as you live; women out, minors in)', 'exam': 'emor exam module fall_festivals_file (Mishnah Sukkah 2:4, 2:6, 2:8)'}
 E passover_in_its_time {'en': "the Passover in its appointed time — the STATUS the people's keeping of the Passover writes on them (the value the date kept): the ink's own phrase for the first Passover's timeliness — 'in its appointed time' (Num 9:2, 9:3, 9:7, 9:13) — and the ledger fact the Sifrei's disparagement reads (67:1: the only Passover of the forty years, Amos 5:25) and the readback will query (Joshua 5:10 the next one, at Gilgal)", 'he': 'אֶת הַפָּסַח בְּמוֹעֲדֽוֹ (the Passover in its appointed time — Num 9:2) · וַיַּעֲשׂוּ אֶת הַפֶּסַח בָּרִאשׁוֹן (and they kept the Passover in the first [month] — Num 9:5)', 'ledger_op': 'status', 'ink': "Num 9:2-3, 9:5 (the command and the keeping), 9:7, 9:13 ('in its appointed time'); Exod 12:28 (the Passover of Egypt kept); Sifrei Bamidbar 65:1 (the appointed time overrides the Sabbath and impurity), 67:1 (the one Passover); Joshua 5:10 [IMPORT] (Gilgal — the next); Amos 5:25 [IMPORT]", 'corpus': 'num_09_pesach_cloud (STEP_Nm_9_5; claim NM09-04)', 'exam': 'law_pesach_sheni (cold_run_pesach_sheni.py) on passover_kept; the sequence tape at Num 9:5'}
a statute kind row (second_tithe_declared): {'en': "the second tithe declared — 'TITHE, YOU SHALL TITHE all the yield of your seed that comes out of the field year by year; and you shall eat before the LORD your God in the place which He will choose to make His name dwell there, the tithe of your grain, your wine and your oil, and the firstlings of your herd and your flock, that you may learn to fear the LORD your God all the days. And when the way is too long for you … then you shall turn it into money, and bind up the money in your hand, and go to the place … and you shall spend the money for whatever your soul desires, for cattle or sheep, for wine or strong drink … and you shall eat there before the LORD your God and rejoice, you and your household; and the Levite who is in your gates, you shall not forsake him, for he has no portion or inheritance with you' (Deut 14:22-27) — NAMED THE SECOND BY THE SHELF (105:2; Numbers 18's first tithe by CALL — korach.the_tithe: tithe_granted on the Levites UNMOVED): the line writes second_tithe_owed, a NEW STATUS on Israel — THE LIABILITIES FROM THE VERSE'S CLAUSES inside the value (105:1-19 — 'the yield of your seed', 'the field', 'year by year': Mishnah Maasrot 1:1, 1:3, 2:4, 4:5-6; the liability by the house or the courtyard from 14:29's 'in your gates' — Bava Metzia 88a:1-2, korach.the_tithe('liable_produce') by CALL; Leviticus 27:30 by CALL temurah.tithe), THREE CONDITIONS FOR THE EATING — the wall of Jerusalem with its TWO CAPACITIES (106:3; Mishnah Zevachim 5:8; Maaser Sheni 3:5-7; Makkot 20a:7 — eating Torah law, admission rabbinic), the House standing (106:4; Temurah 21a:17), the year passed no bar (106:5; Zevachim 29b:2), and THE EXILE'S ARM — no Temple: the tithe left to rot, buried with its hide (Maaser Sheni 1:5-6, the third state as chapter 12's slaughter law had); THE SECOND TITHE HEAVEN'S PROPERTY as ruled (Kiddushin 54b:4; Maaser Sheni 1:1's four bars); the firstling at 14:23 by CALL (ordinances.firstling; korach.the_gifts; Bekhorot 34a-35a), the firstling from outside the Land not brought (106:2; Temurah 21b:3); 'that you may learn to fear' the effect's ground (106:6); THE FAR PLACE of place not time, any distance, the rich too (107:1-3; 12:21's clause by CALL); THE MONEY'S FORM A PARAMETER the_moneys_form (107:4 — R. Yishmael the blank / R. Akiva the imprint at Bava Metzia 47b:5; Mishnah Eduyot 3:2; THE POSSESSION CLAUSE — Mishnah Maaser Sheni 1:2, Bava Kamma 98a:4); Shiloh and the eternal House (107:6 — the eras table by CALL); THREE MONEYS THE LAW'S TABLE (107:7 — Mishnah Maaser Sheni 3:10); THE CLASS FROM THE FOUR NAMED BY GENERAL-PARTICULAR-GENERAL (14:26 — 107:8-11, I6 checked in MIDDOT.md: Bava Kamma 54b:20; NAZIR 35b:3 THE CHAPTER'S VERSE THE SOURCE OF THE METHOD) with water and salt out (Maaser Sheni 1:5, 1:7, 2:1; Eruvin 26b:18) and the containers (107:12-15; Eruvin 27b:3; Maaser Sheni 1:3-4, 3:12-13); THE REJOICING — rejoicing_before_the_lord_commanded REUSED, a SECOND ENTRY on Israel (12:7's the first; 107:16 — I2 with 27:7 ahead, the rejoicing peace offerings); THE LEVITE — levite_forsaking_barred REUSED, a SECOND ENTRY (12:19's the first; 108:1 THE LADDER OF FOUR — 10:9, 12:12, Numbers 18:20-24, 14:29 by CALL)", 'he': 'עַשֵּׂר תְּעַשֵּׂר אֵת כָּל תְּבוּאַת זַרְעֶךָ הַיֹּצֵא הַשָּׂדֶה שָׁנָה שָׁנָֽה (tithe, you shall tithe all the yield of your seed that comes out of the field year by year — Deut 14:22) · וְאָכַלְתָּ לִפְנֵי יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ בַּמָּקוֹם אֲשֶׁר יִבְחַר לְשַׁכֵּן שְׁמוֹ שָׁם מַעְשַׂר דְּגָֽנְךָ תִּֽירֹשְׁךָ וְיִצְהָרֶךָ וּבְכֹרֹת בְּקָרְךָ וְצֹאנֶךָ לְמַעַן תִּלְמַד לְיִרְאָה אֶת יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ כָּל הַיָּמִֽים (the verse continues — Deut 14:23) · וְכִֽי יִרְבֶּה מִמְּךָ הַדֶּרֶךְ כִּי לֹא תוּכַל שְׂאֵתוֹ כִּֽי יִרְחַק מִמְּךָ הַמָּקוֹם אֲשֶׁר יִבְחַר יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ לָשׂוּם שְׁמוֹ שָׁם כִּי יְבָרֶכְךָ יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ (the verse continues — Deut 14:24) · וְנָתַתָּה בַּכָּסֶף וְצַרְתָּ הַכֶּסֶף בְּיָדְךָ וְהָֽלַכְתָּ אֶל הַמָּקוֹם אֲשֶׁר יִבְחַר יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ בּֽוֹ (the verse continues — Deut 14:25) · וְנָתַתָּה הַכֶּסֶף בְּכֹל אֲשֶׁר תְּאַוֶּה נַפְשְׁךָ בַּבָּקָר וּבַצֹּאן וּבַיַּיִן וּבַשֵּׁכָר וּבְכֹל אֲשֶׁר תִּֽשְׁאָלְךָ נַפְשֶׁךָ וְאָכַלְתָּ שָּׁם לִפְנֵי יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ וְשָׂמַחְתָּ אַתָּה וּבֵיתֶֽךָ (the verse continues — Deut 14:26) · וְהַלֵּוִי אֲשֶׁר בִּשְׁעָרֶיךָ לֹא תַֽעַזְבֶנּוּ כִּי אֵין לוֹ חֵלֶק וְנַחֲלָה עִמָּֽךְ (the verse continues — Deut 14:27)', 'form': 'statute', 'witness': ['Deut 14:22 | עשר תעשר את כל תבואת זרעך היצא השדה שנה שנה', 'Deut 14:23 | ואכלת לפני יהוה אלהיך במקום אשר יבחר לשכן שמו שם מעשר דגנך תירשך ויצהרך ובכרת בקרך וצאנך למען תלמד ליראה את יהוה אלהיך כל הימים', 'Deut 14:24 | וכי ירבה ממך הדרך כי לא תוכל שאתו כי ירחק ממך המקום אשר יבחר יהוה אלהיך לשום שמו שם כי יברכך יהוה אלהיך', 'Deut 14:25 | ונתתה בכסף וצרת הכסף בידך והלכת אל המקום אשר יבחר יהוה אלהיך בו', 'Deut 14:26 | ונתתה הכסף בכל אשר תאוה נפשך בבקר ובצאן וביין ובשכר ובכל אשר תשאלך נפשך ואכלת שם לפני יהוה אלהיך ושמחת אתה וביתך', 'Deut 14:27 | והלוי אשר בשעריך לא תעזבנו כי אין לו חלק ונחלה עמך', 'Num 18:21 | ולבני לוי הנה נתתי כל מעשר בישראל לנחלה חלף עבדתם אשר הם עבדים את עבדת אהל מועד', 'Lev 27:30 | וכל מעשר הארץ מזרע הארץ מפרי העץ ליהוה הוא קדש ליהוה', 'Deut 12:17 | לא תוכל לאכל בשעריך מעשר דגנך ותירשך ויצהרך ובכרת בקרך וצאנך וכל נדריך אשר תדר ונדבתיך ותרומת ידך', 'Deut 12:18 | כי אם לפני יהוה אלהיך תאכלנו במקום אשר יבחר יהוה אלהיך בו אתה ובנך ובתך ועבדך ואמתך והלוי אשר בשעריך ושמחת לפני יהוה אלהיך בכל משלח ידך', 'Deut 12:19 | השמר לך פן תעזב את הלוי כל ימיך על אדמתך'], 'ink': "Deut 14:1-29; Onkelos Deut 14:1-29 (the export's chapter 14 the DB's — twenty-nine verses in both numberings); the Sifrei on Deuteronomy ON THE CHAPTER — piska 96's rows 9-12 (14:1) and piskaot 97-110 (the spine whole; the heads not in verse order) with the three rows elsewhere citing the chapter (76:7, 228:5, 312:1); the exam's docket deu_14_reeh_exam_2026-09-21.md (991 rows — link 144 in 38 works, topic 847; LAW 188, DERIVATION 394, DISPUTE 117, CONTEXT 109, OUTSIDE 183; 220 carried, 771 read whole in two runs)", 'corpus': 'deu_14_food_tithe (STEP_Dt_14_1 through STEP_Dt_14_29; claims DV14-01 through DV14-07)', 'tape': "submitted by cold_run_food_tithe.py [subjects: moses (to israel)] (the narrative scene, THE DEUTERONOMY WALK 12b); re-submitted on the sequential tape by cold_run_sequence.py; consumed by law_food_tithe (cold_run_food_tithe.py) -> second_tithe_owed (a NEW STATUS — the liabilities, the three conditions with the exile's arm; the_moneys_form a parameter) and rejoicing_before_the_lord_commanded REUSED and levite_forsaking_barred REUSED (second entries on israel_people — 14:26's and 14:27's seats) on israel_people; at the counter's day (40, 11, 1), no marker", 'fields': ['the_tithe', 'the_place', 'the_far_place', 'the_money', 'the_rejoicing', 'the_levite']}
==== E. THE CALENDAR ====
 C festival_dates = {'value': {'passover': {'month': 1, 'day': 14}, 'passover_1': {'month': 1, 'day': 15}, 'passover_7': {'from': 'passover_1', 'plus': 6}, 'passover_sheni': {'month': 2, 'day': 14}, 'atzeret': {'from': 'omer', 'plus': 49}, 'rosh_hashanah': {'month': 7, 'day': 1}, 'yom_kippur': {'month': 7, 'day': 10}, 'sukkot_1': {'month': 7, 'day': 15}, 'shemini': {'from': 'sukkot_1', 'plus': 7}, 'sabbath': {'key': 'week'}}, 'channel': 'ink', 'source': "Lev 23:5 'in the first month, on the fourteenth of the month, between the evenings, a Passover to the LORD' (passover); 23:6 'on the fifteenth day of this month the feast of unleavened bread' with 23:7 'on the first day a holy convocation' (passover_1); 23:8 'on the seventh day a holy convocation' — the seventh of 23:6's seven days (passover_7 = passover_1 + 6); 23:15-16 'from the morrow of the Sabbath... seven complete weeks... until the morrow of the seventh Sabbath you shall count FIFTY days' — the omer day counted first, the fiftieth sanctified (atzeret = omer + 49; the omer's own day is the row omer_day); 23:24 'in the seventh month, on the first of the month' (rosh_hashanah); 23:27 'on the tenth of this seventh month' (yom_kippur); 23:34 'on the fifteenth day of this seventh month' (sukkot_1); 23:36 'on the eighth day a holy convocation... an assembly' (shemini = sukkot_1 + 7); 23:3 'six days shall work be done and on the seventh day a Sabbath of solemn rest' (sabbath = the Calendar's week). The months in the calendar's own numbering — Exod 12:2 'this month is for you the head of months' (Nisan the first); Num 9:11 'in the second month, on the fourteenth day, between the evenings' (passover_sheni — THE TENT sitting 2, 2026-09-09)", 'teacher': None, 'exercised_by': ['moadim', 'pesach_sheni']}
 C omer_day = {'value': {'month': 1, 'day': 16}, 'channel': 'received', 'source': "Lev 23:11 'on the morrow of the SABBATH the priest shall wave it' (ממחרת השבת) READ as the morrow of the FESTIVAL — the sixteenth of the first month: Sifra Emor Chapter 12 (the four routes); Menachot 65a-66a (the Sages against the Boethusians); the runner's morrow_reading cell graded on Mishnah Chagigah 2:4 (Atzeret can fall beside the Sabbath — so the morrow is the festival's)", 'teacher': 'Sifra Emor Chapter 12; Menachot 65a-66a', 'settings': {'sages': {'month': 1, 'day': 16}, 'boethusians': 'the Sunday after the Sabbath of the festival week — the refused reading (Menachot 65a), UNEXERCISED'}, 'exercised_by': ['moadim']}
